ctcdecode: build as C++17

Why: PyTorch >= 2.1 headers require C++17 (the unpatched build fails with
'#error C++17 or later compatible compiler is required to use PyTorch'), but
ctcdecode c90ad94 hardcodes -std=c++14. Under C++17 its pinned KenLM
submodule (35835f1) then fails with 'ISO C++17 does not allow dynamic
exception specifications' at exactly these five declarations; the
throw(SpecialWordMissingException) specifications are removed. They only
constrain which exception may escape and change nothing for code that throws
the listed type. KenLM is used only for LM rescoring, which CorrNet does not
use. No decoder logic is touched.
Applies to: https://github.com/parlance/ctcdecode @ c90ad94a0b19554f80804fb7812f2a1447a34a70 (patch -p1 from the repo root)
---
diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index a89f24a..5358408 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@ def compile_test(header, library):
     return os.system(command) == 0
 
 
-compile_args = ["-O3", "-DKENLM_MAX_ORDER=6", "-std=c++14", "-fPIC"]
+compile_args = ["-O3", "-DKENLM_MAX_ORDER=6", "-std=c++17", "-fPIC"]
 ext_libs = []
 if compile_test("zlib.h", "z"):
     compile_args.append("-DHAVE_ZLIB")
